{
  "dom_id": "step-q236318",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to the ratio $36:${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the ratio equivalent to $9:2$, we multiply both numbers by the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,9 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,36 &  & : &  & \\,\\boxed{} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get $36$ from $9,$ we multiply $9$ by $4.$ So, to get $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ from $2,$ we multiply $2$ by $4$ as well:\n\n$$\n4\\times 2=8\n$$\n\nThe ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to $36:8.$",
